# CQ 25: Which real-time capability is stated, and what is it bound to?
#
# 351-54-06. Real time is the capability of a system to keep tasks in a runnable
# state so that they react within a pre-determined time interval, not a property
# of time itself. The pattern follows that reading, so the capability is
# instantiated and the interval stated separately as a characteristic value.
PREFIX iec60050:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#>
PREFIX inst: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050/instances#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
SELECT ?item ?capability
WHERE {
  ?item iec60050:hasProperty ?capability .
  ?capability a iec60050:RealTimeCapability .
} ORDER BY ?item
